.TH SOCKET 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
socket \- create a socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B int socket(int domain, int type, int protocol);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a Linux socket in the specified address family, type and protocol.
The header defines AF_UNIX, AF_INET, AF_INET6, SOCK_STREAM, SOCK_DGRAM,
SOCK_NONBLOCK and SOCK_CLOEXEC. Protocol zero selects the default.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a descriptor, or \-1 and sets errno on failure.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bind (3crunch), 
.BR connect (3crunch),
.BR socket (2)
